.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH snakepit 1  "snakepit 0.2.1" 
.SH NAME
snakepit \- 🐍 A dynamic Rust\-based Python dependency installer
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsnakepit\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
🐍 A dynamic Rust\-based Python dependency installer
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
snakepit\-install(1)
📦 Install a Python package
.TP
snakepit\-uninstall(1)
🗑️  Uninstall a Python package
.TP
snakepit\-list(1)
📋 List installed packages with sizes
.TP
snakepit\-sync(1)
🔄 Sync dependencies from requirements file
.TP
snakepit\-search(1)
🔍 Search for packages on PyPI
.TP
snakepit\-show(1)
🔎 Show package details
.TP
snakepit\-init(1)
🚀 Initialize a new project
.TP
snakepit\-venv(1)
🏠 Virtual environment management
.TP
snakepit\-daemon(1)
👹 Daemon management
.TP
snakepit\-fix(1)
🔧 Fix a broken command by analyzing its error output
.TP
snakepit\-fangs(1)
🦷 Hallucinatory Fangs — modify module behavior safely
.TP
snakepit\-snake(1)
🐍 Solid Snake — test on Android devices
.TP
snakepit\-snapshot(1)
📸 Manage package snapshots
.TP
snakepit\-ui(1)
🖥️  Launch the visual dependency dashboard
.TP
snakepit\-run(1)
▶️  Run a command in the snakepit Python environment
.TP
snakepit\-env(1)
⚙️  Show or manage the persistent snakepit environment
.TP
snakepit\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH VERSION
v0.2.1
